const KBEAUTY_GLASSKIN = {"id":"glassskin","emoji":"🪞","hero":{"kicker":"The aspirational K-beauty look, decoded","title":"Glass Skin Method","korean":"유리 피부 / 물광 피부","sub":"Glass skin is luminous, ultra-hydrated, see-through-clear skin. It isn't a product — it's a layering technique. Here's the exact protocol: how to hydrate on damp skin, how many toner layers (the named 7-skin method) for YOUR skin type, the ingredient stack, and realistic timelines.","disclaimer":"Glass skin describes a cosmetic, hydrated finish — not a medical outcome. Results vary; these steps support skin's look and feel, they do not treat skin conditions."},"principles":[{"id":"damp","emoji":"💧","title":"Hydrate on damp skin","body":"Humectants (HA, glycerin, betaglucan) pull water from whatever's nearest. On damp skin they pull moisture IN; on bone-dry skin in low humidity they can pull it OUT. Apply each watery layer while the last is still slightly tacky."},{"id":"thin","emoji":"🪶","title":"Many thin layers, not one thick one","body":"The glass-skin signature is depth of hydration, built by layering several lightweight watery products rather than one heavy cream. Thin layers absorb; thick layers pill and sit on top."},{"id":"order","emoji":"🔢","title":"Thinnest → thickest","body":"Move from the most watery (toner) to the most emollient (cream, then SPF or sleeping mask). Water can't penetrate an oil layer applied first."},{"id":"seal","emoji":"🔒","title":"Always seal the water in","body":"Humectant layers without an occlusive/emollient seal can evaporate and leave skin tight. The final cream (AM) or sleeping mask (PM) locks the hydration in — this is the step most people skip."},{"id":"press","emoji":"🤲","title":"Press, don't rub","body":"Pat each layer in with warm palms or press with fingertips. Rubbing causes pilling and disrupts the layer underneath."},{"id":"spf","emoji":"☀️","title":"Glass skin lives and dies by SPF","body":"All the hydration in the world looks dull under UV damage, and brightening progress reverses without it. Daily SPF 50+ PA++++ is non-negotiable for the clear, even tone half of the look."}],"sevenSkin":{"title":"The 7-Skin Method (7스킨법)","what":"A Korean technique where you layer a hydrating toner (\"skin\" is the Korean word for toner) multiple times — pressing each layer in before the next — to flood skin with lightweight hydration. \"7\" is the famous number, not a rule: you tune the count to your skin and the weather.","how":"Use a hydrating, alcohol-free toner (look for HA, glycerin, betaglucan, panthenol — not an exfoliating/astringent toner). Dispense into palms or a cotton pad, press over the face, wait ~20–30 seconds until tacky, repeat. Stop while skin still feels comfortable, never sticky or overloaded.","tonerType":"Must be a HYDRATING toner. Never use a low-pH exfoliating toner (AHA/BHA) or an alcohol-forward astringent toner for this — repeated layering of acids or alcohol will over-exfoliate and damage the barrier.","layersBySkin":[{"skin":"dry","layers":"5–7","note":"Dry and dehydrated skin benefits most from the full method. Layer generously, then seal hard with a ceramide cream. In winter, slug on top."},{"skin":"normal","layers":"3–5","note":"A comfortable middle ground for plump, dewy skin without heaviness."},{"skin":"combination","layers":"3–4","note":"Go heavier on dry cheeks, lighter on the oily T-zone. You can layer fewer times in the T-zone."},{"skin":"oily","layers":"2–3","note":"Use a watery, oil-free toner and fewer layers — over-layering can feel greasy and congest. Hydration still matters: dehydrated oily skin overproduces oil."},{"skin":"sensitive","layers":"2–3","note":"Fewer layers of a fragrance-free, minimal-ingredient toner (betaglucan/panthenol/centella). Patch test first; build up slowly."}],"mistakes":["Using an exfoliating or alcohol toner instead of a pure hydrating one — the #1 way to wreck your barrier chasing glass skin.","Layering on dry skin in a dry room — seal each round before it fully evaporates.","Skipping the final cream/occlusive — water layers alone evaporate and leave skin tighter than before.","Adding 7 layers when your skin only wants 3 — stickiness, pilling and clogged pores follow. More layers ≠ more glass."]},"protocol":{"title":"The glass-skin protocol","intro":"An AM and a PM sequence. The AM build is about a dewy, protected daytime glow; the PM build is about deep overnight repair. Tune the 7-skin layer count to your skin type above.","am":[{"n":1,"step":"Gentle low-pH cleanse","emoji":"🧼","ing":[],"why":"Start with a clean, slightly damp face — don't strip. Leave skin barely towel-patted, not bone dry.","routineRef":"watercleanse"},{"n":2,"step":"7-skin hydrating toner layers","emoji":"💦","ing":["hyaluronic","betaglucan","panthenol"],"why":"The hydration base. Press in your skin-type's layer count of a watery, alcohol-free toner.","routineRef":"toner"},{"n":3,"step":"Glow essence","emoji":"🌿","ing":["galactomyces","rice","snail"],"why":"A ferment/rice/snail essence on still-damp skin adds the luminous, bouncy depth that reads as 'glass'.","routineRef":"essence"},{"n":4,"step":"Brightening + plumping serum","emoji":"🍊","ing":["vitaminc","niacinamide"],"why":"Vitamin C + niacinamide even tone and add antioxidant defense — the 'clear & even' half of glass skin. (Use vitamin C in the AM.)","routineRef":"treatment"},{"n":5,"step":"Lightweight gel-cream seal","emoji":"🧴","ing":["ceramide","squalane"],"why":"Seal all that water in with a non-heavy cream so it doesn't evaporate. Don't skip this.","routineRef":"moisturizer"},{"n":6,"step":"SPF 50+ PA++++","emoji":"☀️","ing":[],"why":"Glass skin is impossible to maintain without it — UV dulls tone and undoes brightening. Reapply midday.","routineRef":"sunscreen"}],"pm":[{"n":1,"step":"Double cleanse","emoji":"🫗","ing":[],"why":"Oil cleanser to melt SPF/makeup, then a gentle water cleanser. A truly clean canvas is what lets layers absorb.","routineRef":"oilcleanse"},{"n":2,"step":"7-skin hydrating toner layers","emoji":"💦","ing":["hyaluronic","betaglucan"],"why":"Rebuild the hydration base at night, when skin repairs and absorbs most.","routineRef":"toner"},{"n":3,"step":"Repair essence / first essence","emoji":"🍶","ing":["galactomyces","snail","propolis"],"why":"Press a ferment/snail/propolis layer into damp skin for overnight glow and bounce.","routineRef":"essence"},{"n":4,"step":"Treatment (alternate nights)","emoji":"🧪","ing":["pdrn","peptides","retinol"],"why":"On repair nights, a PDRN/peptide ampoule for bounce; on separate nights, a slow-introduced retinol for long-term clarity & texture (PM only, then SPF next day).","routineRef":"treatment"},{"n":5,"step":"Barrier cream","emoji":"🧱","ing":["ceramide","panthenol"],"why":"A richer ceramide cream at night locks everything in and rebuilds the barrier that holds water.","routineRef":"moisturizer"},{"n":6,"step":"Optional: sleeping mask / slug (dry skin)","emoji":"🌙","ing":["squalane"],"why":"For very dry skin or winter, a thin occlusive sleeping-mask layer maximizes overnight hydration — wake up to plump, glassy skin.","routineRef":"sleeping"}]},"ingredientStack":{"title":"The glass-skin ingredient stack","intro":"These cross-reference the Ingredient Encyclopedia — tap any to learn more. The look is built on hydrators + brighteners + barrier-sealers.","groups":[{"id":"hydrate","label":"Hydrate & plump","emoji":"💧","ings":["hyaluronic","betaglucan","panthenol","snail"]},{"id":"glow","label":"Glow & ferment","emoji":"✨","ings":["galactomyces","rice","propolis"]},{"id":"brighten","label":"Brighten & even","emoji":"🍊","ings":["vitaminc","niacinamide"]},{"id":"bounce","label":"Bounce & firm","emoji":"🐟","ings":["pdrn","peptides"]},{"id":"seal","label":"Seal the barrier","emoji":"🧱","ings":["ceramide","squalane"]}]},"timeline":{"title":"Realistic timelines — what to actually expect","intro":"Glass skin builds in stages. Hydration shows up fast; tone and clarity take real consistency. Anyone promising it overnight is selling, not informing.","stages":[{"id":"instant","when":"Same day","emoji":"⚡","headline":"Instant dewy plump","body":"Right after layering, skin looks dewier and feels bouncier. This is surface hydration — real, but it resets daily. Consistency is what makes it stick."},{"id":"hydration","when":"2–4 weeks","emoji":"🌱","headline":"Hydration holds","body":"With daily layering + sealing, your skin's hydration baseline rises. Tightness fades, makeup sits better, the dewy look lasts through the day rather than disappearing by noon."},{"id":"tone","when":"2–3 months","emoji":"🌟","headline":"Tone & clarity even out","body":"Brightening actives (vitamin C, niacinamide) + diligent SPF gradually even tone and fade marks. This is the 'see-through clarity' half of glass skin — and it only sticks with sun protection."},{"id":"texture","when":"3–6 months","emoji":"🪞","headline":"Refined, glassy texture","body":"Gentle exfoliation + retinoids/peptides over time refine the look of pores and texture, so light reflects more evenly. Slow and steady beats over-exfoliating, which sets you back."}],"honestNote":"Pore size, genetics and skin conditions set a ceiling — 'poreless' glass-skin photos are usually good lighting, hydration and sometimes makeup. The realistic, sustainable goal is YOUR skin, hydrated, even and healthy. If a concern (persistent acne, melasma) isn't improving, see a dermatologist."},"shelf":{"title":"Shop your glass-skin shelf","intro":"The full glass-skin layering kit in one basket — a hydrating toner, a glow essence, an HA serum and a sealing cream (add SPF + a sleeping mask to complete it).","items":[{"id":"toner","label":"Hydrating toner (for 7-skin)","emoji":"💦","seed":"korean hydrating toner hyaluronic 7 skin alcohol free"},{"id":"essence","label":"Glow essence","emoji":"🌿","seed":"korean essence galactomyces rice glow"},{"id":"serum","label":"HA / plumping serum","emoji":"💧","seed":"korean hyaluronic acid serum hydrating"},{"id":"cream","label":"Ceramide sealing cream","emoji":"🧱","seed":"korean ceramide moisturizer barrier cream"},{"id":"spf","label":"SPF 50+ PA++++","emoji":"☀️","seed":"korean sunscreen spf50 pa beauty of joseon"},{"id":"mask","label":"Sleeping mask (seal/slug)","emoji":"🌙","seed":"korean sleeping mask overnight hydration"}],"bundleSeed":"korean glass skin set toner essence hyaluronic serum cream"}};
